      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im looking at this house contract in seattle and i keep seeing the word \"escrow\" everywhere. im kinda lost. can u basically explain what an escrow agent actually does and why they need to hold my money for a while? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow in a real estate contract, especially in a place like Seattle, is a process that makes the transaction safe for everyone involved. Think of the escrow agent as a neutral, highly trusted third party, like a specialized banker for the deal. They are responsible for holding your funds and the property documents until *all* the agreed-upon conditions of the sale have been met. This prevents one party from getting the money and then running off with the property, which is a huge risk, and it keeps the whole process from falling apart halfway through.",
